# KNOWN GAP — `Box[float32]` READS ZERO on the C lane and will not BUILD on
# the LLVM lane. The allocator's NAME and its BODY disagree about how wide the
# element is.
#
# The element name is derived correctly: `c_type_name_for_id(F32_TYPE)` is
# `"float"`, which is the right C spelling, and the emitted call really is
# `__gorget_box_alloc_float`. The BODY generated for that name is
#
#     static inline void* __gorget_box_alloc_float(double val) {
#         double* p = (double*)GORGET_ALLOC(sizeof(double)); *p = val; ... }
#
# — eight bytes, storing a `double`. The reader is `*(float *)(p)`, four bytes.
# The value is written as a `double` and read back as a `float`: the low four
# bytes of `1.5` are all zero, so C prints `0.000000` with `gg check` clean.
# LLVM's typed IR sees the same disagreement and refuses at `llc`
# (`call ptr @__gorget_box_alloc_float(double %v2)`), which is exactly the
# signature of the element-type collapse the ten-primitive fixture closed —
# here on the one arm that fixture does not cover.
#
# ⚠ MEASURED ON BOTH SIDES OF THAT FIX, so nobody reads this as a regression
# it is not: identical before and after — C build rc 0 / run rc 0 / prints
# `0.000000`, LLVM build rc 1. The `float32` arm was never reached by the
# element-naming fix.
#
# ⚠ MECHANISM, and it is a Layering rule 1 loss rather than a naming bug:
# `emit_runtime_helpers` (`src/backend/c_lir/emit_types.rs`) types the helper's
# parameter with `box_alloc_inner_c_type`, which for a primitive IGNORES the
# name suffix and uses the LIR param type instead — and the LIR param type has
# already widened the `f32` to `double`. `box_alloc_suffix_to_c_type`, right
# beside it in `helpers.rs`, maps `"float"` correctly; the emitter just does
# not ask it on this path. The f32-ness survives in the NAME and is gone from
# the LIR type, and the emitter trusts the lossy one.
#
# ⛔ DISCRIMINATORS, so this is not lumped with its neighbours:
#   * NOT the element-type collapse that
#     `tests/fixtures/box_ctor_primitive_element_types.gg` pins. That was the
#     NAME axis — every unnamed element collapsing onto `Box__int64_t`. Here
#     the name is RIGHT and the body is wrong, which is precisely why a
#     ten-cell net over the other primitives cannot see it.
#   * NOT the missing type check at consuming positions
#     (`known_gaps/float32_consuming_positions_accept_float_literal.gg`).
#     THAT is why this fixture writes `1.5 as float32` rather than a bare
#     `1.5`: the cast makes the source genuinely `float32`, so the checker has
#     nothing to say and the emitter defect is the ONLY one left standing. A
#     repro written with a bare literal exercises both and adjudicates neither.
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT (what the language SHOULD do): 1.500000
# EXPECTED EXIT: 0, on BOTH backends.

void main():
    float32 x = 1.5 as float32
    Box[float32] a = Box[float32](x)
    print((*a))
